4	// csrc/fused/gfx942/opt_components.hip.hpp — REAL per-optimizer device-function
5	// composition library for the gfx942 fused L3/L1 megakernel (Phase 3 cont.).
6	//
7	// The AMD twin of csrc/fused/sm_90/opt_components.cuh. It eliminates the gfx942
8	// false positive (the demo's 4-optimizer opt_update + AdamW fallback for the
9	// other 7). Every one of the 11 optimizers here has its OWN real per-element
10	// update — transcribed byte-faithfully from the canonical reference math in
11	// csrc/algorithms/<opt>.h (adamw_step / lion_step / grokfast_fused_step /
12	// grokadamw_step / looksam_apply_step / prodigy_apply_step /
13	// neuralgrok_apply_step+psi_forward / muon_update_step / sg11_sweep_b_step /
14	// sg15_sweep_b_step + sg15_alpha_per_coord). NO fallback, NO templating one
15	// optimizer from another.
16	//
17	// WHY transcribed (not #included): csrc/algorithms/<opt>.h pulls
18	// csrc/common/platform.h whose GROK_HIP branch includes <thrust/...>, which the
19	// free-standing AMDGCN device gate (scripts/amdgcn_check.sh, no ROCm/thrust)
20	// cannot resolve. The math is duplicated verbatim here for per-file self-
21	// containment (an explicitly-accepted trade) and is gate-compilable with clang
22	// __builtin_* math. A parity test against the algorithm headers is the CPU/
23	// MI300X oracle item in HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md.
24	//
25	// Compiled by the DEVICE pass only (__AMDGCN__ gate, or __HIPCC__).
26	// ============================================================================
